   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **In Chains**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 11 archived performances [3]\n- **An Ocean Between the Waves**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Holding On**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **Knocked Down**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Nothing To Find**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 12 archived performances [3]\n- **Up All Night**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **You Don't Have To Go**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Clean Living**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Pain, Strangest Thing [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **wod2017-09-19.terminal5_acidjack** (recommended): audience recording; 15 songs; 108 min [1]\n- **TheWarOnDrugs2017-09-19.nyctaper**: audience recording; 15 songs; 108 min [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **wod2017-09-19.terminal5_acidjack**: taped by acidjack; transferred by acidjack; source: Digital Audience [1]. Also: Final output is FLAC level 8, transferred from WAV via Audacity [1]\n- **TheWarOnDrugs2017-09-19.nyctaper**: taped by nyctaper; transferred by nyctaper; source: AUD [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by Toby Tenenbaum: [The War on Drugs began NYC stay at Terminal 5 (pics, videos, setlist)](https://www.brooklynvegan.com/the-war-on-drugs-began-nyc-stay-at-terminal-5-pics-videos-setlist/) [4]\n- Poster by Toby Tenenbaum: [The War on Drugs began NYC stay at Terminal 5 (pics, videos, setlist)](https://www.brooklynvegan.com/the-war-on-drugs-began-nyc-stay-at-terminal-5-pics-videos-setlist/) [5]",
